up-type="author"><name><surname>Akpinar</surname><given-names>E</given-names></name><name><surname>Turkbey</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Ozcan</surname><given-names>O</given-names></name><name><surname>Akdogan</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Karcaaltincaba</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Ozen</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Bilateral scrotal extraperitoneal herniation of ureters: computed tomography urographic findings and review of the literature</article-title><source>J Comput Assist Tomogr</source><year>2005</year><volume>29</volume><fpage>790</fpage><lpage>792</lpage></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Akpinar E, Turkbey B, Ozcan O, Akdogan B, Karcaaltincaba M, Ozen H (2005) Bilateral scrotal extraperitoneal herniation of ureters: computed tomography urographic findings and review of the literature. J Comput Assist Tomogr 29:790&#x02013;792 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16272853</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR10"><label>10.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Alam</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Nice</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Uberoi</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The accuracy of ultrasound in the diagnosis of clinically occult groin hernias in adults</article-title><source>Eur Radiol</source><year>2005</year><volume>15</volume><fpage>2457</fpage><lpage>2461</lpage></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Alam A, Nice C, Uberoi R (2005) The accuracy of ultrasound in the diagnosis of clinically occult groin hernias in adults. Eur Radiol 15:2457&#x02013;2461 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15986204</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR11"><label>11.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Al